---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getDocsUrl } from "../lib/docs";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Caelix · Structured Rust services"
  description="Caelix gives Rust backend applications clear, explicit structure through modules, services, and controllers."
>
  <main class="home" data-pagefind-body>
    <section class="home-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A Rust backend framework</p>
        <h1>Give your Rust services a clear architecture.</h1>
        <p class="home-lede">
          Caelix gives backend applications a clear, explicit structure: modules
          compose the system, services own the work, and controllers expose it.
        </p>
        <div class="home-actions">
          <a
            class="button button-primary"
            href={getDocsUrl("getting-started/overview")}>Get started →</a
          >
          <a
            class="button button-secondary"
            href="https://github.com/Ohanronnie/caelix">View on GitHub ↗</a
          >
        </div>
        <div class="install-command" aria-label="Install Caelix CLI">
          <b>$</b><code>cargo install caelix-cli</code><button
            type="button"
            data-copy-command="cargo install caelix-cli">Copy</button
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="architecture-card" aria-label="Caelix application structure">
        <div class="architecture-top">
          <i></i><i></i><i></i><span style="margin-left: .35rem"
            >src/app.module.rs</span
          >
        </div>
        <pre
          class="architecture-code"><code><span class="accent">use</span> caelix::&#123;Module, ModuleMetadata&#125;;

<span class="accent">pub struct</span> AppModule;

<span class="accent">impl</span> Module <span class="accent">for</span> AppModule &#123;
    <span class="accent">fn</span> register() <span class="accent">-&gt;</span> ModuleMetadata &#123;
        ModuleMetadata::new()
            .provider::&lt;UsersService&gt;()
            .controller::&lt;UsersController&gt;()
    &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="path-section" aria-labelledby="paths-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A framework for application code</p><h2
            id="paths-title"
          >
            Start small. Stay organized.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Build a minimal route, then bring in the boundaries your application
          needs—without losing a clear picture of how it fits together.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="path-grid">
        <a
          class="path-card"
          href={getDocsUrl("getting-started/minimal-application")}
          ><span>01</span><strong>Create an application →</strong><p>
            Start with a module and a controller.
          </p></a
        >
        <a class="path-card" href={getDocsUrl("concepts/modules")}
          ><span>02</span><strong>Compose with modules →</strong><p>
            Keep imports and registrations visible.
          </p></a
        >
        <a class="path-card" href={getDocsUrl("advanced/microservices")}
          ><span>03</span><strong>Extend the system →</strong><p>
            Add events, gateways, and microservices.
          </p></a
        >
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="path-section" aria-labelledby="explore-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Explore Caelix</p><h2 id="explore-title">
            Useful paths through the framework.
          </h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="path-grid path-grid--explore">
        <a class="path-card" href={getDocsUrl("concepts/providers")}
          ><span>Providers</span><strong>Typed dependency injection →</strong><p
          >
            Make dependencies explicit and testable.
          </p></a
        >
        <a class="path-card" href={getDocsUrl("concepts/controllers")}
          ><span>Controllers</span><strong>Routes and request handling →</strong
          ><p>Keep transport concerns at the edge.</p></a
        >
        <a class="path-card" href={getDocsUrl("advanced/openapi")}
          ><span>Tooling</span><strong>OpenAPI and Swagger UI →</strong><p>
            Document the API your application exposes.
          </p></a
        >
        <a class="path-card" href={getDocsUrl("why-caelix/overview")}
          ><span>Why Caelix</span><strong>Choose your backend boundary →</strong
          ><p>See what Caelix shares across Actix and Axum.</p></a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
